# iac-private

Private inventories, host variables, and secrets for the public
[iac](https://github.com/NGenetzky/iac) automation repository.

Generated by `iac`'s `ansible/iac-private-init` scaffold. Nothing in this
repo should be pushed to a public remote.

## Layout

- `inventories/` - one directory per environment.
{% for inv in iac_private_scaffold_inventories %}
  - `inventories/{{ inv.name }}` ({{ inv.type }}) - {{ inv.description }}
{% endfor %}
- `docs/` - private notes and generated documentation.

## Usage

Clone the public `iac` repo as a sibling directory (or add it as a git
submodule at `../iac`) so each inventory's `ansible.cfg` / `.debops.cfg`
can reference its roles and playbooks.

Encrypt real secrets with `ansible-vault` before committing, even though
this repository is private.
